Committed as c09152ca. Here's what landed and what I actually watched happen.

## What shipped

The alarm (src/format/cost.rs, in the existing #[cfg(test)] mod tests): price_drift_audit_against_models_dev, #[ignore]d on purpose, fetches https://models.dev/api.json via curl --max-time 60 --fail, parses ["deepseek"]["models"] with the existing serde_json, and compares the three cells both sides carry — table (input, cache_read, output) vs the vendor's — over every vendor id model_pricing resolves. cache_write is printed as skipped (no counterpart; DeepSeek bills reads only) and reasoning is never read (it duplicates output). It panics with a "DID NOT RUN … UNVERIFIED" message on fetch or parse failure, and its failure text says explicitly: read the vendor's page, do not auto-patch the constants, do not edit this test to agree.

The register, with a shrink-only ratchet. KNOWN_DIVERGENCES admits deepseek-v4-pro (models.dev {0.435, 0.87, 0.003625} vs table (0.27, 1.10)) with a checkable reason, and registered_divergences_still_diverge (a non-ignored test) fails if the reason is not a real sentence, if the id is listed twice, if the table stops pricing it, or if it stops diverging — plus it is printed as skipped on every audit run rather than dropped silently.

The offline arm, which is the testability decision rather than a style choice. The comparison is a pure function audit_vendor_rows driven by the vendored MODELS_DEV_DEEPSEEK_2026_09_20 const, so the comparison half is covered by the default suite — an alarm whose only covered step was its own curl would be nearly unverified. parse_models_dev_deepseek returns Err, never an empty Ok, for a missing provider/models/cost cell.

Wired into `skills/release/SKILL.md` — both the "Gate (ALL must pass)" list and "How to check" gained cargo test price_drift_audit -- --ignored, with the instruction to read it, not just pass it.

## Verification actually run

• `cargo test` → green, 17 test binaries, no failures; the ignored audit never runs there, which is the point.
• `cargo test price_drift_audit -- --ignored --nocapture → **green**, and I recorded the live output: compared 3 row(s): ["deepseek-flash", "deepseek-v4-flash", "deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp"], deepseek-v4-pro reported as the admitted skipped divergence, and the coverage limit printed (deepseek-r1, deepseek-v3` are **audited by nothing** — I confirmed both are absent from models.dev's listing). So task 1's correction is confirmed against the vendor, not just against its own literal.
• **Positive controls, serially, each one atomic mutate → run → restore:** `0.60 → 0.61` on the flash output cell reddened it naming all three Flash aliases with both readings (`table (0.15, 0.003, 0.61) vs models.dev (0.15, 0.003, 0.6)); emptying KNOWN_DIVERGENCES reddened it naming deepseek-v4-pro`. Both restored to a byte-empty diff, green again.
• `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings → clean (two errors found and fixed along the way: unused_mut on a closure, cloned_ref_to_slice_refs). cargo fmt then cargo fmt -- --check` → clean.
• `tests/module_size.rs register pasted 2931 → 3439` in the same diff; the gate went fatal at +511 before I did, which is the gate working.

## Limits, stated rather than implied

One aggregator (models.dev can itself be wrong — hence a human decision, not a patch); DeepSeek-only population, and deepseek-r1/deepseek-v3 are audited by nothing; peak pricing unmodelled on both sides, so a correct row is still a lower bound. Not done and named: #937's option 3 (pushing non-Anthropic prices upstream into yoagent) needs a yoagent release first, and no user override was added — model_pricing_with already provides override > preset > table. No CLAUDE.md change, as specified.
